# Optional: UpComputer Connect source builds
# Leave these unset to disable UpComputer Connect in local source builds.
# Release builds inject their public values at build time. These are public
# identifiers, not secrets. Do not add server-side secrets to this file.
# Each name also works with the upstream T3CODE_ prefix. See
# docs/operations/upcomputer-connect-setup.md.

# Get these from the Clerk Dashboard under API keys, JWT templates, and OAuth applications.
# UPCOMPUTER_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_...
# UPCOMPUTER_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE=upcomputer-relay
# UPCOMPUTER_CLERK_CLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=...

# Optional: signed macOS passkey builds. The RP domain defaults to the Frontend API
# hostname encoded in the Clerk publishable key. Set the override only when Clerk
# returns a different RP ID or when multiple domains must be entitled.
# UPCOMPUTER_APPLE_TEAM_ID=ABC1234567
# UPCOMPUTER_MACOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE=/absolute/path/to/upcomputer.provisionprofile
# UPCOMPUTER_CLERK_PASSKEY_RP_DOMAINS=example.clerk.accounts.dev,clerk.example.com

# The UpComputer Connect relay. `infra/relay` deploys update it automatically.
# UPCOMPUTER_RELAY_URL=https://relay.<api-zone>

# Optional: hosted app origin used by the CLI's out-of-band OAuth flow.
# Defaults to https://up.computer.
# UPCOMPUTER_HOSTED_APP_URL=https://up.computer
